{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Greatest Common Factor of Terms.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Greatest Common Factor of Terms.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"greatest common factor of terms greatest common factor of terms","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Greatest Common Factor of Terms.md","fileName":"Greatest Common Factor of Terms.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Greatest Common Factor of Terms","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Factoring and Algebraic Identities]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","Monomial","Polynomial Factorization","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Greatest Common Factor of Terms.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Greatest Common Factor of Terms.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"greatest common factor of terms greatest common factor of terms","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Greatest Common Factor of Terms.md","fileName":"Greatest Common Factor of Terms.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Greatest Common Factor of Terms","heading":"Greatest Common Factor of Terms","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The greatest common factor of algebraic terms is the largest [[Monomial]] that divides every term. Its numerical coefficient is the greatest common divisor of the coefficients, and each shared variable uses the smallest exponent appearing across the terms.\n\nFor (20a^2b^3+24a^3b^2), the greatest common factor is (4a^2b^2). Variables missing from any term cannot appear in the common factor. Extracting this factor first simplifies later [[Polynomial Factorization]] and reveals the remaining structure.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","Monomial","Polynomial Factorization","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Greatest Common Factor of Terms.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Greatest Common Factor of Terms.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"greatest common factor of terms greatest common factor of terms","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Greatest Common Factor of Terms.md","fileName":"Greatest Common Factor of Terms.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Greatest Common Factor of Terms","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","Monomial","Polynomial Factorization","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}